# the-wheel-changes-the-view — BACKLOG C7, and it is `@D002`'s own
# proposed gate, built.
#
# ⚠⚠ **The defect it closes: `cam.zoom` changed no pixel.**  The wheel
# moved it from plan 01, `save.loft` persisted it, and `snap`'s state
# line reported it — while every file that drew anything took the base
# `VIEW_PPM` as a constant, so the picture was **identical at `z1` and
# at `z6`**.  ⚠ `PROBLEMS.md` called it Med rather than Low for exactly
# the reason this file exists: scenarios already walked the camera to a
# zoom and `at` already asserted it arrived, so **the gate was green
# over a control that did nothing**.
#
# ── ⚠⚠ Why SHARES and not a snap ────────────────────────────────
#
# `@D002` named the shape before the fix existed: *two snaps of one map
# at two zooms, and `classify_world` shares that DIFFER — a golden would
# agree with whatever it started drawing.*  That is `CLAUDE.md` § A
# golden AGREES WITH A SHEAR said in advance, so every reading below is
# a share of the canvas and none of them is an image.
#
# ── What it reads ───────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# One 13x13 patch of grass, photographed from three distances.  The
# share falls by roughly a QUARTER each time the zoom doubles, because a
# share is an AREA and the scale is `VIEW_PPM / zoom` in both directions
# at once — which is the half a "they differ" reading cannot see.

echo the wheel changes the view: one map, three distances

at 0 0 1

palette 5
drag -6 -6 6 -6
drag -6 -5 6 -5
drag -6 -4 6 -4
drag -6 -3 6 -3
drag -6 -2 6 -2
drag -6 -1 6 -1
drag -6 0 6 0
drag -6 1 6 1
drag -6 2 6 2
drag -6 3 6 3
drag -6 4 6 4
drag -6 5 6 5
drag -6 6 6 6
count painted 169 169

# ⚠⚠ **The closest view — the number every other gate in the tree was
# sized at.**  If this one ever moves, C7 has changed the game rather
# than the wheel.
frame grass 0.206 0.209
snap c7_the_wheel_z1

# Twice as far out: a quarter of the pixels, because a share is an area.
at 0 0 2
frame grass 0.051 0.054
snap c7_the_wheel_z2

# ⚠ And `@D002`'s own example, four times out — the reading that was
# bit-for-bit identical to the first one before this shipped.
at 0 0 4
frame grass 0.012 0.015
snap c7_the_wheel_z4

# ⚠ Back to the closest view, and the share comes back exactly: the
# wheel is a SCALE and not a crop, so nothing about the world moved.
at 0 0 1
frame grass 0.206 0.209
count painted 169 169
